sentences.l:
And the high stair she mounted of her own house,
and she took a well-bent key in her thick hand,
fine, of bronze;

who him, being a guest-friend, killed in his own house,
cruel, nor the retribution of the gods did he revere, nor the table,
the one, his own, that he had set beside him;

at once then she the strap swiftly loosed from the handle,
and in the key she sent, and she drove back the bolts of the doors,
aiming straight at them;

And she, when now she reached the suitors, heavenly-one of women,
stood then beside the doorpost of the close-built roof,
before her cheeks holding her shining veil;

“Hear me, lordly suitors, you who this house
have pressed upon, to eat and to drink continually, always,
the man having been gone a long time;

